{
    "name": "E2E SAP Emarsys - Find Contacts",
    "description": "End-to-end test for the SAP Emarsys connector - looks a contact up by an exact match on the e-mail field.",
    "notes": {
        "28ca6f52-abc5-4d78-970f-736ff80028a2": {
            "x": 64,
            "y": 32,
            "width": 928,
            "height": 208,
            "content": "## ⚠️ Test data assumption - the contact must already exist\n\nFind Contacts matches **exactly** on one indexed contact field; here on E-mail (field id `3`).\nThis connector has no Create Contact component and contact creation is a non-default Emarsys\npermission, so the flow cannot seed its own data.\n\n1. In Emarsys, create or pick a contact and note its e-mail address.\n2. Open the **Set Variable** node and set `contactEmail` to that address.\n3. Grant the API credential `field.list`, `contact.list` (contact/query) and `contact.getdata`\n   under Management > Security Settings > API Credentials.\n\nOnly indexed columns can be filtered - id, uid, email (3) and externalId are indexed by default.\nAn unknown value leaves through the `notFound` port and the flow stalls until AfterAll times out."
        }
    },
